                  <xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="printHydFile">
                    <xs:annotation>
                      <xs:documentation>This is the printHydFile parameters group. printHydFile generates the hydrodynamic database (hyd-file).</xs:documentation>
                    </xs:annotation>
                    <xs:complexType>
                      <xs:all>
                        <xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="includeAddDamping">
                          <xs:simpleType>
                            <xs:annotation>
                              <xs:documentation>The user may specify the 'includeAddDamping' (boolean) switch. If &quot;true&quot; is selected, then the additional damping from DBRESP (if any) will be added to the potential damping and written to the hyd-file. If &quot;false&quot; is selected then only the potential damping is written to the hyd-file. (default value = false)</xs:documentation>
                            </xs:annotation>
                            <xs:restriction base="xs:boolean">
                              <xs:pattern value="^ *true|TRUE|1|false|FALSE|0 *$"/>
                            </xs:restriction>
                          </xs:simpleType>
                        </xs:element>
                        <xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="includeIncWaveForces">
                          <xs:simpleType>
                            <xs:annotation>
                              <xs:documentation>The user may specify the 'includeIncWaveForces' (boolean) switch. If &quot;true&quot; is selected, then the forces due to the incoming wave are included in the hyd-file (FAMP, FEPS RECORDS). If &quot;false&quot; is selected then the forces due to the incoming wave are excluded from the hyd-file (only diffraction forces remain). This should be done when incoming wave forces are computed by other means (i.e. Froude Krylov option in aNySIM). (default value = true)</xs:documentation>
                            </xs:annotation>
                            <xs:restriction base="xs:boolean">
                              <xs:pattern value="^ *true|TRUE|1|false|FALSE|0 *$"/>
