            <xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="parDBDRIFT">
              <xs:annotation>
                <xs:documentation>This is the DBDRIFT parameters group. DBDRIFT computes the mean wave drift forces by means of pressure integration and by means of the Faltinsen-Michelsen method.</xs:documentation>
              </xs:annotation>
              <xs:complexType>
                <xs:all>
                  <xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="1" name="runProgram">
                    <xs:simpleType>
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The user must specify the 'run program' (boolean) switch. If &quot;true&quot; is selected, then the program DBDRIFT will be run. If &quot;false&quot; is selected the program DBDRIFT is not run. (default value = false)</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                      <xs:restriction base="xs:boolean">
                        <xs:pattern value="^ *true|TRUE|1|false|FALSE|0 *$"/>
                      </xs:restriction>
                    </xs:simpleType>
                  </xs:element>
                  <xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="exportPressuresAndVelocities">
                    <xs:simpleType>
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The user may specify the 'exportPressuresAndVelocities' (boolean) switch. If &quot;true&quot; is selected, then the wave pressures and velocities are exported. If false is selected, then the wave pressures and velocities are not exported. (default value = false)</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                      <xs:restriction base="xs:boolean">
                        <xs:pattern value="^ *true|TRUE|1|false|FALSE|0 *$"/>
                      </xs:restriction>
                    </xs:simpleType>
                  </xs:element>
                  <xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="exportContribution1">
                    <xs:simpleType>
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The user may specify the 'exportContribution1' (boolean) switch. If &quot;true&quot; is selected, then contribution 1 (due relative wave elevation on the waterline) of the drift forces is exported. If false is selected, then contribution 1 is not exported. (default value = false)</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                      <xs:restriction base="xs:boolean">
                        <xs:pattern value="^ *true|TRUE|1|false|FALSE|0 *$"/>
                      </xs:restriction>
                    </xs:simpleType>
                  </xs:element>
                  <xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="exportContribution2">
                    <xs:simpleType>
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The user may specify the 'exportContribution2' (boolean) switch. If &quot;true&quot; is selected, then contribution 2 (due to square of water velocities on the hull) of the drift forces is exported. If false is selected, then contribution 2 is not exported. (default value = false)</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                      <xs:restriction base="xs:boolean">
                        <xs:pattern value="^ *true|TRUE|1|false|FALSE|0 *$"/>
                      </xs:restriction>
                    </xs:simpleType>
                  </xs:element>
                  <xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="exportContribution3">
                    <xs:simpleType>
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The user may specify the 'exportContribution3' (boolean) switch. If &quot;true&quot; is selected, then contribution 3 (due to rotation of first-order forces) of the drift forces is exported. If false is selected, then contribution 3 is not exported. (default value = false)</xs:documentation>
