                    <xs:simpleType>
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The user may specify the method to compute the wave drift forces, either fast but memory intensive (CPU_priority) or slower but memory-saving (RAM_priority) (value list = CPU_priority, RAM_priority) (default value = RAM_priority)</xs:documentation>
                      </xs:annotation>
                      <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
                        <xs:whiteSpace value="collapse"/>
                        <xs:enumeration value="CPU_priority"/>
                        <xs:enumeration value="RAM_priority"/>
                      </xs:restriction>
                    </xs:simpleType>
                  </xs:element>
                  <xs:element maxOccurs="1" minOccurs="0" name="exportQTFtoVTK">
                    <xs:simpleType>
                      <xs:annotation>
                        <xs:documentation>The user may specify the 'exportQTFtoVTK' (boolean) switch. If &quot;true&quot; is selected, then the mean drift force QTF (all 6 modes) on each body is exported to a vtk file (one file per frequency) for visualisation. If &quot;false&quot; is selected the the QTF is not exported. (default value = false)</xs:documentation>
